# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# architecture-standards-init-example — every environment variable, by tier.
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) only if you are running the scripts that read one.
# The application itself does NOT read this file: locally its secrets come from
# `dotnet user-secrets` via AppHost parameters, and in deployment from Fly
# secrets (P5). The journey a value takes is documented once, in flyio/SECRETS.md.
#
# Tiers
#   always   the system will not do its job without it
#   mode     selects a behaviour; has a documented default
#   secret   a credential; never committed, never in [env] in a fly.toml
#   ci       consumed only by GitHub Actions, stored in a GitHub Environment
#   tuning   optional; absence degrades a named feature rather than failing (P8)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- mode -------------------------------------------------------------------

# Selects the persistence provider. With no value AND no connection string the
# service falls back to the in-memory provider, which is what makes `git clone &&
# dotnet run` work with zero credentials (P4, P8).
#   PostgreSQL | SqlServer | (unset -> InMemory)
# Degrades without it: nothing. You get an in-memory database that is empty on
# every restart — correct for tests and a first run, wrong for anything you want
# to keep.
DATABASE_PROVIDER=

# ASP.NET Core hosting environment. Default: Development locally, Production in
# the containers (set in each fly.toml's [env]).
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development


# --- secret -----------------------------------------------------------------

# The API's own database. This is the ONLY database credential the API holds; it
# has no credentials for any other database, so splitting the shared Postgres
# instance into per-service instances later is configuration, not code (P3).
#
# Local:    generated into `dotnet user-secrets` by scripts/setup.sh — you do not
#           set this by hand, and you should not invent a value (IDENTITY §10:
#           a human asked to make up a secret produces `changeme`).
# Deployed: a Fly secret, assembled by the deploy workflow from POSTGRES_PASSWORD.
# Degrades without it: falls back to InMemory. Data does not survive a restart.
ConnectionStrings__apidb=

# The Postgres superuser password for the shared instance. Root secret: it lives
# in the GitHub Environment and the workflow derives every connection string from
# it, so no per-service credential is stored anywhere (FLY-IO §9).
# Generate hex or alphanumeric only — `+`, `/`, `=` and `;` all mean something
# inside a connection string (IDENTITY §10).
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=


# --- ci ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# Fly.io deploy credential. `fly tokens create org`, stored in the GitHub
# Environment named `dev` — an environment, not a repository secret, because an
# environment can be reviewed and restricted (FLY-IO §11).
# Degrades without it: the deploy workflow fails at the first flyctl call, which
# is the correct place to fail.
FLY_API_TOKEN=

# Fly organisation the apps are created in. Defaults to `personal`.
FLY_ORG=personal


# --- tuning -----------------------------------------------------------------

# OpenTelemetry collector. When set, traces, metrics and logs are exported there
# (P15). The Aspire dashboard sets it for you during local development.
# Degrades without it: telemetry is still collected and still instrumented — it
# is simply not exported anywhere. No feature is lost; observability is.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=

# Azure Monitor. When present, an Azure Monitor exporter is added alongside OTLP.
# Degrades without it: no Azure Monitor export. OTLP is unaffected.
APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING=

# Where the frontend's server side finds the API. Read at REQUEST time by
# /api/config and by the BFF proxy — never baked into the bundle, which is what
# lets one image serve every environment (FRONTEND-BFF §2, P12).
# Degrades without it: the proxy walks its candidate ladder (service discovery ->
# internal DNS -> localhost) and usually still finds the API in development.
API_BASE_URL=

# Comma-separated browser origins allowed to call the API directly. Normally
# EMPTY: the browser talks only to the frontend's own origin, and the frontend's
# server side calls the API (FRONTEND-BFF §1). A value here is a deliberate
# decision to widen that.
Cors__AllowedOrigins__0=
